Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Episode 3: The Prince and the Letter (Hamlet, the first act and the fourth) ──────────────────────────────────
  // The Margravate of Harrowmere. The old Margrave died in his orchard last spring of a bite the physicians cannot
  // find; his brother Rolf wears the chain and has married the widow. The Prince, Tiernan, twenty-one, has been seen
  // on the rampart talking to the dark. The Chancellor hires the company, nominally to play at the court and in fact
  // to keep the Prince alive, which is very difficult, because he is brilliant, reckless, funny and has decided
  // that his own safety is the least interesting thing in the Margravate. Then the Margrave sends the Prince away
  // 'for his health' with a sealed letter to the Margrave of Orlay, to be carried by the company: a letter that
  // says, in the courteous hand of a man ordering a fish, that its bearers are to be put to death. Act II of the
  // King's Players played the third act of this play, as a night of horror; this is its first and its fourth.
  // The company is the means by which the Prince is kept alive, and the means by which he is sent to die; both at once.
  Place harrowmere "Harrowmere" is settlement within wend at 4, 1.
  Place hm_gate "the gate of Harrowmere" is room within harrowmere at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place hm_hall "the great hall of Harrowmere" is room within harrowmere at 1, 1.
  Place hm_rampart "the south rampart" is room within harrowmere at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place hm_study "the Prince's study" is room within harrowmere at 2, 1.
  Place hm_chapel "the chapel" is room within harrowmere at 2, 0.
  Place hm_yard "the tiltyard" is room within harrowmere at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place hm_road "the Orlay road" is room within harrowmere at 0, 3 outdoors.
  Place hm_inn "the Fox and Feather" is room within harrowmere at 1, 3.
  Place or_gate "the gate of Orlay" is room within harrowmere at 2, 3 outdoors.
  Place or_larder "the Orlay larder" is room within harrowmere at 3, 2.
  Place or_hall "the hall of Orlay" is room within harrowmere at 3, 3.
  Passage hmg_hall "the gatehouse arch" is arch between hm_gate and hm_hall.
  Passage hmh_ramp "the south stair" is path between hm_hall and hm_rampart.
  Passage hmh_study "the Prince's door" is door between hm_hall and hm_study.
  Passage hmh_chapel "the chapel door" is door between hm_hall and hm_chapel.
  Passage hmg_yard "the tiltyard path" is path between hm_gate and hm_yard taking 10 minutes.
  Passage hmg_road "the Orlay road" is road between hm_gate and hm_road taking 1 hour.
  Passage hmr_inn "the inn yard" is path between hm_road and hm_inn taking 10 minutes.
  Passage hmr_orlay "the road on to Orlay" is road between hm_road and or_gate taking 2 hours
    opening when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 19 "The road on to Orlay is not walked after dark, and the gate there shuts at dusk. The company can sleep at the Fox and Feather, or in the hedge.".
  Passage org_larder "the larder door" is door between or_hall and or_larder
    opening when e3Unlocked(rierdan) "The larder door is oak, and barred on the outside.".
  Passage org_hall "the gate-hall of Orlay" is arch between or_gate and or_hall.
  Observe hm_gate_scene at hm_gate when true "A castle of the pale local stone, with a portcullis that has not been lowered in thirty years and a flag at half mast that no one has remembered to raise. A stable-boy in the arch is sitting with a book. 'The Prince,' he says, without being asked, 'is on the roof. He is always on the roof.'".
  Observe hm_hall_scene at hm_hall when true "A long hall hung with the old Margrave's banners and the new Margrave's, which are not the same colour. A dais, two chairs, one of them with the cushion still on it. A court that is trying hard not to be seen to watch the door.".
  Observe hm_rampart_scene at hm_rampart when true "A walk on the top of the south wall, wide as a cart, with a view of orchards in the dark. The wind has a voice. There is a cold place by the third merlon where the air is wrong, and a scratch on the stone at the height of a young man's elbow.".
  Observe hm_study_scene at hm_study when true "A room full of books laid open face down, fencing foils, a skull of no obvious provenance, a bust of the Prince's father with a moustache drawn on it in ink and then, plainly, scrubbed off. A window onto the orchard.".
  Observe hm_chapel_scene at hm_chapel when true "A small cold chapel with a stone floor, a stone Margrave on a stone tomb, and a stone Margravine beside him with the space for the next. A single candle. Someone is kneeling at the rail.".
  Observe hm_yard_scene at hm_yard when true "A tiltyard of trodden grass with a rack of blunted foils and a bench where three idle captains drink at ten in the morning.".
  Observe hm_road_scene at hm_road when true "Where the Orlay road leaves the Harrowmere fields: a milestone, a gibbet nobody has used, a pond with a heron.".
  Observe hm_inn_scene at hm_inn when true "A low inn with a stable and a big table, a landlady who counts the room and its secrets by the fire. The sign is a fox in a ruff.".
  Observe or_gate_scene at or_gate when true "Orlay is a wall and a gate and a fat banner of three keys. A guard in the arch stops everyone and asks them a question about their luggage, regardless of what they are carrying.".
  Observe or_hall_scene at or_hall when true "A hall like a larder: hams, cheeses, tapestries of food, and in the middle a small, sharp, kind old woman in a large chair, signing things.".

  Relation e3Orchard(place). Relation e3Trap(place). Relation e3Fumbled(place). Relation e3Spies(place). Relation e3Watched(group). Relation e3PrinceKnows(place). Relation e3Cracked(place). Relation e3ReadTried(place). Relation e3Bellerophon(place). Relation e3Killed(place). Relation e3Explained(place). Relation e3TurnedAway(place). Relation e3Confessed(place). Relation e3On(place). Relation e3Ghost(group). Relation e3Spared(place). Relation e3Letter(place). Relation e3Read(place). Relation e3Forged(place).
  Relation e3Burned(place). Relation e3Kept(place). Relation e3Seized(place). Relation e3Mixed(place). Relation e3Delivered(place).
  Relation e3Grave(place). Relation e3Escape(place). Relation e3Misdelivered(place). Relation e3Done(place).
  Relation x1(place). Relation x2(place). Relation x3(place). Relation x1c(place). Relation x2c(place). Relation x3c(place).
  Relation tiernanTrust(group). Relation tiernanScorn(group). Relation tiernanLonely(group). Relation e3PrinceAlong(place). Relation swaleHand(group). Relation swaleVain(group).
  Measure harm(place). Measure e3LockedAt(place). Measure e3Start(place).

  Person tiernan "Prince Tiernan" at hm_study {
    Role "the Prince of Harrowmere, twenty-one". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "A tall, ink-stained, laughing young man in black, sitting on his desk with his boots on a chair. 'Ah,' says the Prince. 'My bodyguards. How very sad for you. I am the least guardable man in the Margravate; ask anyone. I have been trying to be assassinated since the spring and the court is simply not up to it.'".
  }
  Person rolf "Margrave Rolf" at hm_hall {
    Role "the Margrave of Harrowmere, the Prince's uncle". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "A large, easy man with the Margrave's chain a size too tight. 'My nephew,' says Rolf, 'is a wonderful boy. Keep the boy alive, there's a good fellow, and if you can make him a little less interesting, there is a purse in it. Do what you can.'".
  }
  Person iseult "Margravine Iseult" at hm_hall {
    Role "the Margrave's wife, the Prince's mother". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A woman who has been very beautiful and has decided to be still. 'You are to stand where he can see you,' she says. 'He does not do foolish things where he can see a witness. He does them to prove he is right.'".
  }
  Person fosbury "Chancellor Fosbury" at hm_hall {
    Role "the Chancellor". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "A little man in a very big furred gown who keeps a notebook open on his forearm. 'I have been the Chancellor of three Margraves,' he says, 'and this is the first time one of them has been dead and sitting down. I will pay you thirty pieces. Keep him off the roof.'".
  }
  Person ysenne "Ysenne Fosbury" at hm_chapel {
    Role "the Chancellor's daughter". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A girl of nineteen at the altar rail, who has stopped praying to look at you. 'He says things,' she says, 'that sound like jokes and are not.'".
  }
  Person spargo "Sir Dunmow Spargo" at hm_hall {
    Role "a young courtier of the Prince's, his friend". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A fair young man with an anxious smile and a very new sword. 'The Prince's friend,' he says. 'Dunmow. I am to go with him wherever he goes, which is the one thing, I think, that frightens me.'".
  }
  Person quillan "Sir Cullen Quillan" at hm_hall {
    Role "a courtier, the Prince's friend". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A dark young man who watches you without moving his head. 'Cullen,' he says. 'I am the other.'".
  }
  Person captain "Captain Fenn Darrow" at hm_yard {
    Role "a drunk captain of the guard". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'The Prince!' says Captain Darrow, who is holding two foils and has not noticed. 'Tell the Prince from me, he fences like a poet. I'll fence him like a pig.'".
  }
  Person berengar "Margravine Aldith" at or_hall {
    Role "the Margravine of Orlay". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "A small old woman in a large chair, who looks at you over a pile of letters. 'From Rolf,' she says, tapping the pile. 'Does he think I read these? Sit. You look as if you've been walking.'".
  }

  // The commission: the Chancellor engages the company.
  Topic fosbury_job with fosbury "Ask the Chancellor what he wants of the company" when true once {
    Says "'Of the Players: a play, the Margrave has asked it, and it will be very good for the court's appearance. Of you: that you keep the Prince alive.' He closes the notebook. 'He goes to the south rampart at midnight to speak to what is not there. He fences the captains for money. He prays, and then does not do what he went to the chapel to do. He says he is going to prove a point. I do not know what the point is. The point is a number of people at present, and the Margrave is one of them.'".
    On discuss { Assert e3On(rierdan). Set e3Start(rierdan) to watch(clock). }
  }

  // Swale is sent for: the Prince has written a speech and wants it said by a professional. He comes up from the Wend in the Chancellor's cart.
  Rule e3_swale when e3On(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) and at(party, hm_hall) and troupe(swale) and not at(swale, hm_hall) and at(swale, ?sw) { Retract at(swale, ?sw). Assert at(swale, hm_hall). }
  Observe e3_swale_told at hm_hall when e3On(rierdan) and troupe(swale) and not e3Done(rierdan) "Ambrose Swale has been fetched up from the Fourways in the Chancellor's cart, with his make-up box on his knee, looking as if he had been asked to criticise a ghost.".

  // The Prince is hard to guard. Three exploits, each with a counter, each costing him a harm if the company is absent.
  Rule rp_x1 when e3On(rierdan) and not x1(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 12 {
    Assert x1(rierdan). Retract at(tiernan, hm_study). Assert at(tiernan, hm_rampart). }
  Rule rp_x1h when x1(rierdan) and not x1c(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 18 {
    Assert x1c(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. Retract at(tiernan, hm_rampart). Assert at(tiernan, hm_study). }
  Rule rp_x2 when x1c(rierdan) and not x2(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 30 and at(tiernan, ?q) {
    Assert x2(rierdan). Retract at(tiernan, ?q). Assert at(tiernan, hm_yard). }
  Rule rp_x2h when x2(rierdan) and not x2c(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 36 {
    Assert x2c(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. Retract at(tiernan, hm_yard). Assert at(tiernan, hm_study). }
  Rule rp_x3 when x2c(rierdan) and not x3(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 48 and at(tiernan, ?q) {
    Assert x3(rierdan). Retract at(tiernan, ?q). Assert at(tiernan, hm_chapel). Assert at(rolf, hm_chapel). }
  Rule rp_x3h when x3(rierdan) and not x3c(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 54 {
    Assert x3c(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. Retract at(tiernan, hm_chapel). Assert at(tiernan, hm_study). Retract at(rolf, hm_chapel). Assert at(rolf, hm_hall). }
  Observe x1_told near tiernan when x1(rierdan) and at(tiernan, hm_rampart) "The Prince stands at the third merlon in the dark with his sword out, talking at the air in a voice he has plainly rehearsed. A cold comes up off the stones. Beyond him the orchard glows, faintly, white.".
  Observe x2_told near captain when x2(rierdan) and at(tiernan, hm_yard) and not x2c(rierdan) "The Prince has two foils and a bet of fifty crowns that he can touch the captain before the captain touches him. The captain is much the bigger. He is also drunk, but has not been told that this is the wrong kind.".
  Observe x3_told near tiernan when x3(rierdan) and at(tiernan, hm_chapel) and not x3c(rierdan) "The Margrave kneels at the rail with his back to the room. Behind him the Prince has drawn his sword. He has not moved. He is breathing hard, as if from a long stair.".

  // The counters.
  Action stand_by_prince(actor: group, site: place) "Stand beside the Prince on the rampart and say nothing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_rampart) and at(tiernan, hm_rampart) and x1(rierdan) and not x1c(rierdan).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert x1c(rierdan). Assert tiernanTrust(actor). Assert e3Ghost(actor). }
    Result "You stand a pace behind his elbow. At last he says, without turning, 'You are the first person who has stayed. Everyone else announces they are going to stay, and then does.' The cold place stirs, and takes the shape of an old man with an apple in his hand. It looks past you. It says one sentence to the Prince, who has gone white, and you do not hear it. The cold place goes quiet. When he turns his face is wet and he is grinning. 'I'll need you for the chapel,' he says. 'I mean to behave badly.'".
  }
  Action disarm_captain(actor: group, site: place) "Step between the Prince and the captain, and take the captain's foil" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_yard) and x2(rierdan) and not x2c(rierdan) and not f_capt(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, tumbling, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert x2c(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert f_capt(rierdan). Assert x2c(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "You come in under the captain's arm and the foil is in your hand before either of them has finished the sentence. The captain looks at his empty fingers with deep sorrow. 'I let him have that,' he says. The Prince applauds, once, and says 'Not bad. Not bad at all, for a bodyguard,' and walks off in a better mood than he arrived in.".
    Otherwise "The captain's foil takes you across the ribs in a way that was meant for the Prince. It is blunt. It is a lot of foil.".
  }
  Rule rp_rolf_home when x3c(rierdan) and at(rolf, hm_chapel) { Retract at(rolf, hm_chapel). Assert at(rolf, hm_hall). }
  Rule rp_confess when x3(rierdan) and e3Trap(rierdan) and not x3c(rierdan) { Assert x3c(rierdan). Assert e3Confessed(rierdan). }
  Observe e3_confess_told at hm_chapel when e3Confessed(rierdan) "The Margrave does not pray. He kneels with his hands open and his mouth working, and says to the stone Margrave on the tomb, aloud, clearly: 'I cannot. Brother, I cannot.' Behind him the Prince's sword comes down by itself, an inch at a time, and the Prince sits on the floor of the chapel with his hand over his face.".
  Action stop_chapel(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Prince by the sleeve before he does it" {
    Speaker tiernan.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_chapel) and x3(rierdan) and not x3c(rierdan) and not e3Trap(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert x3c(rierdan). Assert e3Spared(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert x3c(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "'He is at his prayers,' you whisper. 'If you kill him now he goes to the gods clean.' The Prince stares at you. His mouth works. 'You have heard the same story,' he says, with great bitterness, and lowers the sword. 'I'll wait,' he says, 'until he is doing something thoroughly damnable. A man should be caught at his best sin.'".
    Otherwise "'Let go,' says the Prince, in a voice you have not heard. He throws off your hand and goes in with the sword up, and Sir Cullen Quillan, who was in the porch, knocks the blade down and cuts the Prince across the forearm with his own. The Margrave turns on his knees and sees the blood and his nephew's face, and his mouth shuts.".
  }

  Topic tiernan_ghost with tiernan "Ask the Prince what the cold place said to him" when e3Ghost(party) and not e3Orchard(rierdan) once {
    Says "'Orchard,' says the Prince. 'It said, my son, the orchard.' He looks at the skull. 'My father slept in the orchard after dinner, every day of his life. They told me it was a snake. My uncle was the first to find him.' He is still. 'I have only a word. A word is not a proof.'".
    On discuss { Assert e3Orchard(rierdan). }
  }
  Observe tiernan_dark near tiernan when e3On(rierdan) and not x1(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "When you come in the Prince is sitting at his desk in the dark with the skull in his two hands, still. Then he sees you, and the room is full of his laugh again, as if somebody had lit a lamp.".

  // The players' trap: Swale speaks a murder in an orchard, and the Margrave is watched while he hears it.
  Action set_trap(actor: group, site: place) "Have Swale work a speech about a king killed in an orchard into the Prince's play, and watch the Margrave hear it" {
    Speaker swale.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_hall) and at(swale, site) and e3Orchard(rierdan) and not e3Trap(rierdan) and not e3Fumbled(rierdan) and not x3(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert e3Trap(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert e3Fumbled(rierdan). Increase harm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "Swale gives it in the Prince's own lines, to the hall, in a flat reading voice: a sleeper in an orchard, a poured cup, a brother. The Margrave takes his chain in both hands. He does not move. He asks for wine, and does not drink it, and goes out. The Prince, at the back, is breathing hard and has not looked at you once.".
    Otherwise "Swale begins well and then, from habit, adds an ornament. The Margrave smiles at it: a verse is a verse. The Prince, in the corner, closes his eyes.".
  }
  Observe spies_scene near quillan when x1c(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) and not e3Spies(rierdan) "Sir Cullen Quillan is at the Prince's desk turning over the Prince's papers. He puts them down very gently when you look, and goes on being agreeable.".
  Action watch_friends(actor: group, site: place) "Watch the Prince's two friends: where they go when he is not looking" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_hall) and e3On(rierdan) and not e3Watched(actor) and not e3Spies(rierdan).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert e3Watched(actor). Assert e3Spies(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert e3Watched(actor). }
    Result "Sir Dunmow Spargo goes to the Margrave's door every evening with a small, scrupulous face, and stays a quarter of an hour. Sir Cullen Quillan waits in the passage. They are the Prince's friends; they are also, plainly, the Margrave's ears, and neither of them thinks the less of himself for it.".
    Otherwise "They are friendly, and talk of hawks. You learn that Dunmow is afraid of horses.".
  }

  // The Prince asks the company things; the answers are remembered at the road and at the match.
  Topic tiernan_ask with tiernan "Ask the Prince why he talks to the rampart" when e3On(rierdan) and at(tiernan, hm_study) once {
    Says "'Because it answers,' says the Prince. He sits up. 'Here is a thing to be honest about, because otherwise there is no fun in it. If you knew your father had been murdered, and you could not prove it, and the man who did it was kind to you at supper: what would you do?'".
  }
  Topic tiernan_a1 with tiernan "Wait, and watch, and be sure" answering tiernan_ask when true {
    Says "'Sensible,' says the Prince, with enormous disappointment. 'I was afraid you would say that. It is what everyone says. It is what I have been doing for six months.' He looks at the skull. 'It is dreadful.'".
    On discuss { Assert tiernanScorn(actor). }
  }
  Topic tiernan_a2 with tiernan "Make him show it: a play, a trap, a trick" answering tiernan_ask when true {
    Says "The Prince leaps off the desk. 'THAT,' he says. 'Yes. A play. I had a play in mind and could not decide who to trust to put on a play.' He grabs your hands. 'You are the Players! You are the PLAYERS!' His face falls. 'Oh. I have done it again. I have given a plan to the person who is hired to stop me.'".
    On discuss { Assert tiernanTrust(actor). }
  }
  Topic tiernan_a3 with tiernan "Leave. Go somewhere he cannot be kind to you at supper" answering tiernan_ask when true {
    Says "The Prince is silent. 'That,' he says at last, 'is the one I could not do. Not because I am brave. Because I do not know where I would be if I were not here.' He glances at the skull. 'Everyone thinks I stay for revenge. I stay because I haven't got anywhere else I am a prince.'".
    On discuss { Assert tiernanLonely(actor). }
  }
  Topic swale_prince with swale "Ask Swale to speak the Prince's lines to him as a player would" when e3On(rierdan) and at(swale, hm_hall) once {
    Says "Swale rolls up a sleeve. 'The Prince has written a speech,' he says, 'and asked that I show him how to say it.' He turns to the empty hall. 'To be or not to be,' he begins, and stops. 'No. He writes better than that. It is, I regret to say, better.' He looks at you, stricken. 'Do I tell him it wants cutting?'".
  }
  Topic swale_cut with swale "Tell him it wants no cutting; he is the better writer" answering swale_prince when true {
    Says "Swale sits down heavily. 'Yes,' he says. 'Thank you.' For the first time he looks at a younger writer without malice.".
    On discuss { Assert swaleHand(actor). }
  }
  Topic swale_vain with swale "Tell him it wants cutting, and cut it" answering swale_prince when true {
    Says "'Of course,' says Swale, happily, and goes off to cut the Prince's best line to ribbons, which the Prince will not forgive.".
    On discuss { Assert swaleVain(actor). }
  }

  // The letter.
  Kind rolf_letter "the Margrave's letter to Orlay" is document teaching letter_read described "A single folded sheet, sealed with the Margrave's own signet in green wax, addressed in the Chancellor's fair hand: To my good neighbour the Margravine of Orlay, by the hand of the Players and my nephew.".
  Discovery letter_read "The Margrave's letter, read: 'Dear neighbour, receive the bearers kindly and see to it that none of them is alive by the end of the week, beginning with my nephew. R.'".
  Rule rp_letter when x3c(rierdan) and not e3Letter(rierdan) and harm(rierdan) < 3 and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 60 {
    Assert e3Letter(rierdan). Give rolf_letter to party. Assert at(tiernan, hm_hall). Assert at(spargo, hm_hall). Assert at(quillan, hm_hall). }
  Observe letter_told at hm_hall when e3Letter(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "The Margrave has given the company a sealed letter for Orlay, 'a courtesy,' and sent his nephew along for his health. Sir Dunmow Spargo and Sir Cullen Quillan are to go as well, to see the Prince comfortable, with a smaller packet of their own. Nobody looks at the Chancellor, who is looking at the floor.".
 
  Action read_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Warm the seal over a candle and read the Margrave's letter" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and e3Letter(rierdan) and holding(actor, rolf_letter) and not e3ReadTried(rierdan).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, trapwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert e3Read(rierdan). Assert e3ReadTried(rierdan). Assert knows(actor, letter_read). }
    On failure { Assert e3Cracked(rierdan). Assert e3ReadTried(rierdan). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3 or to nothing. }
    Result "The wax lifts in one piece, the way it does when the man who sealed it did not expect it to be lifted. The letter is a courteous page of the Margrave's best phrases, and in the middle of it, between a remark on the weather and one on the price of wool, it asks that its bearers be killed. It does so in the voice of a man ordering a fish.".
    Otherwise "The wax cracks across the signet. You hold it over the candle until it runs, and press it shut with the flat of a knife, and the Margrave's seal now has a seam in it that a child could see. You did not learn what it said, and the cook who lent the candle is owed three crowns for forgetting that he did.".
  }
  Kind second_sheet "a sheet of the Prince's good paper" is document described "A clean sheet of the Prince's cream paper, with his crest in the corner and a chewed quill-mark.".
  Action take_sheet(actor: group, site: place) "Take a clean sheet of the Prince's paper from his desk" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_study) and e3Letter(rierdan) and not holding(actor, second_sheet) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3SheetTaken(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    On success { Give second_sheet to actor. Assert e3SheetTaken(rierdan). }
    Result "The Prince watches you take it. After a moment he pushes the ink an inch toward you.".
  }
  Action tell_prince_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Prince what his uncle's letter says, and what you might do with it" {
    Speaker tiernan.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tiernan, site) and e3Read(rierdan) and not e3PrinceKnows(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert e3PrinceKnows(rierdan). }
    Result "He reads it over your arm. 'Ask for them,' he says, evenly. 'Dunmow and Cullen. If it must be somebody's name, let it be somebody I know.' He gives a short laugh. 'Do not tell me it is not what you meant.'".
  }
  Action forge_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Swale to write a new letter in the Margrave's hand, in place of the old" {
    Speaker swale.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and e3Read(rierdan) and e3PrinceKnows(rierdan) and holding(actor, second_sheet) and at(swale, site) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3Burned(rierdan).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert e3Forged(rierdan). Spend second_sheet from actor. }
    On failure { Spend second_sheet from actor. }
    Result "Swale takes the seal, a pen and a scruple of the Margrave's best ink, and for twenty minutes is not an actor but a clerk. The new letter asks the Margravine of Orlay, with the Margrave's compliments, to receive Sir Dunmow Spargo and Sir Cullen Quillan very kindly, and to see that they are not alive at the end of the week. He signs it with a flourish. 'Why,' he says, 'that is the best part I have had since Lear.'".
    Otherwise "'Oh,' says Swale, looking at his work, 'oh dear. That is the Duke of Pentrice's hand. I was thinking of someone else.' The sheet is spoiled.". 
  }
  Action burn_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Burn the Margrave's letter in the nearest hearth" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, hm_inn) or at(actor, hm_hall)) and e3Letter(rierdan) and e3Read(rierdan) and holding(actor, rolf_letter) and not e3Burned(rierdan) and not e3Forged(rierdan).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert e3Burned(rierdan). Spend rolf_letter from actor. }
    Result "It goes up in a small bright flower. The Prince, who is watching, applauds. 'Beautifully done. A little late, but the form was perfect.'".
  }
  Action seal_letter_away(actor: group, site: place) "Wrap the letter in oilskin and keep it on your own person" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and e3Letter(rierdan) and holding(actor, rolf_letter) and not e3Kept(rierdan) and not e3Mixed(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert e3Kept(rierdan). }
    Result "You wrap it in oilskin and tie it about your waist under your coat. Pudding, who has been carrying every other parcel for a week, looks briefly relieved and then cross.".
  }
  Relation e3MixRolled(place).
  Rule rp_mix when e3Letter(rierdan) and at(party, hm_inn) and not e3MixRolled(rierdan) and not e3Mixed(rierdan) and not e3Kept(rierdan) and not e3Burned(rierdan) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 9 and dice(clock) <= 10 {
    Assert e3MixRolled(rierdan). Assert e3Mixed(rierdan). Spend rolf_letter from party. }
  Rule rp_mix_safe when e3Letter(rierdan) and at(party, hm_inn) and not e3MixRolled(rierdan) and not e3Mixed(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 9 and dice(clock) > 10 { Assert e3MixRolled(rierdan). }
  Observe e3_mix_told at hm_inn when e3Mixed(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "In the grey of the morning Jem Pudding picks up every parcel in the room, humming, and puts them in the Orlay basket. The Margrave's letter is among them. So is Hepzibah's laundry list. And a love-poem of Kit's, the one he did not mean anyone to read. By the time anyone counts, the basket is on a carrier's cart and the cart is on the road.".
  Observe e3_mix_safe_told at hm_inn when e3MixRolled(rierdan) and not e3Mixed(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "In the grey of the morning Jem Pudding goes round the room with the Orlay basket, humming, and gathers every parcel but the one you are sitting on.".
  Hazard road_cutpurse "The Orlay road at night" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule rp_road_night at hm_road when e3Letter(rierdan) and at(party, hm_road) and not e3Robbed(rierdan) and (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 5) and dice(clock) <= 9
    says "Two men step out of the hedge with the sort of cudgels that are carried for effect, and mean it." {
    Assert e3Robbed(rierdan). Assert strikes(road_cutpurse, party). }
  Relation e3Robbed(place).
  Rule rp_to_orlay when e3Letter(rierdan) and at(party, or_gate) and not e3PrinceAlong(rierdan) { Assert e3PrinceAlong(rierdan). Assert at(tiernan, or_gate). Assert at(spargo, or_gate). Assert at(quillan, or_gate). }

  // At Orlay: what the Margravine does with what she is handed. Five shapes of arrival.
  Action confront_margrave(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the Margrave's own letter, sealed, on the table before him in front of the court" {
    Speaker rolf.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hm_hall) and at(rolf, hm_hall) and e3Read(rierdan) and e3Kept(rierdan) and holding(actor, rolf_letter) and not e3Done(rierdan) and not f_conf(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert e3Exposed(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). Spend rolf_letter from actor. }
    On failure { Assert f_conf(rierdan). Assert e3Dismissed(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
    Result "You lay it down, sealed, with his own signet on it, and say what it asks, and of whom. The court has stopped breathing. The Margrave looks at the green wax for a long moment, and then at his nephew, and takes it up and puts it in the fire himself. 'It is a courtesy,' he says, 'that was not meant.' Nobody in the hall will say what it was meant for. He sends the Prince to his mother, and goes out.".
    Otherwise "'My seal,' says the Margrave, pleasantly, 'on a thing you were not to open. You have been very diligent.' He takes it from you. The court watches the company go out of the hall; by morning the company's wagon is on the road with a guard beside it.".
  }
  Observe e3_exposed_told near rolf when e3Exposed(rierdan) "The Margrave has not come out of his rooms. The Chancellor says the court is in mourning for something it cannot name, and has paid the company in full, in advance, to be gone by dawn.".
  Observe e3_dismissed_told at hm_hall when e3Dismissed(rierdan) "The hall is cold and the Prince is not in it. The Chancellor will not meet your eye as he counts out the fee.".
  Action present_forged_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Hand the Margravine of Orlay the letter that Swale wrote" {
    Speaker berengar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, or_hall) and at(berengar, or_hall) and e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3Delivered(rierdan) and not e3Misdelivered(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert e3Delivered(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert e3Delivered(rierdan). Assert e3ForgeBlown(rierdan). }
    Result "The Margravine reads it twice. You stand very straight and look like people who have been sent with a letter.".
    Otherwise "She reads it, and then holds the signature against a letter of the Margrave's she keeps in her sleeve. The two hands do not agree about the loop of an R.".
  }
  Action present_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Hand the Margravine of Orlay the letter you were given" {
    Speaker berengar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, or_hall) and at(berengar, or_hall) and e3Letter(rierdan) and holding(actor, rolf_letter) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3Mixed(rierdan) and not e3Delivered(rierdan) and not e3Misdelivered(rierdan) and not e3Burned(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert e3Delivered(rierdan). }
    Result "The Margravine reads it twice, with her lips moving. She looks up. Her face does not alter. 'Leave it with me,' she says.".
  }
  Action present_the_basket(actor: group, site: place) "Present what the carrier brings: the basket of parcels" {
    Speaker berengar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, or_hall) and at(berengar, or_hall) and e3Mixed(rierdan) and not e3Delivered(rierdan) and not e3Misdelivered(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert e3Misdelivered(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
    Result "The Margravine opens the first parcel and reads the laundry list, and the second and reads Kit's love-poem aloud, with feeling, and the third. 'My neighbour,' she says, 'has written me the most remarkable letter of my life. I do not understand a word of it, but I think I am being courted.' She sends a ham.".
  }
  Rule rp_orlay_cracked when e3Delivered(rierdan) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and e3Cracked(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) { Assert e3Escape(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). Assert e3CrackedSaved(rierdan). Assert e3Held(rierdan). Assert at(tiernan, or_hall). }
  Rule rp_orlay_forged when e3Delivered(rierdan) and e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3ForgeBlown(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) { Assert e3Escape(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). Assert e3Seized(rierdan). Assert e3Killed(rierdan). }
  Rule rp_orlay_blown when e3Delivered(rierdan) and e3ForgeBlown(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) { Assert e3Bellerophon(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
  Rule rp_orlay_genuine when e3Delivered(rierdan) and not e3Forged(rierdan) and not e3Cracked(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) { Assert e3Bellerophon(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
  Relation e3CrackedSaved(place).
  Observe e3_held_told at or_hall when e3Held(rierdan) "The Prince is staying. The Margravine has not made it a threat: he will be her guest until the Margrave his uncle has sent to ask for him, and nobody expects the Margrave to ask. The company is free to go. The Prince walks you to the gate and stands in it for a little.".
  Observe e3_cracked_told at or_hall when e3CrackedSaved(rierdan) "The Margravine turns the sheet over and sees the seam in the seal. She turns it in the light. 'This has been opened,' she says, 'and closed by somebody who does not do it for a living.' She does not ask what it said. 'I should not like to have to act on a letter I cannot swear to. Go out by the kitchen. Run.'".
  Observe e3_forged_told at or_hall when e3Seized(rierdan) "The Margravine reads it, and looks at the two young men in the doorway, who are smiling at her, and says: 'Seize them.' She looks at you. 'The Margrave my neighbour has never been so definite.'".
  Observe e3_blown_told at or_hall when e3ForgeBlown(rierdan) "The Margravine folds the letter in four, and then in eight. 'That is a clever hand,' she says, 'but I have had thirty years of his R. I do not like to be written to by a boy.' She makes a small sign, and the guards close the door.".
  Observe e3_genuine_told at or_hall when e3Bellerophon(rierdan) and not e3ForgeBlown(rierdan) "The Margravine reads it twice, with her lips moving. Her face does not alter. 'My neighbour is very clear,' she says. 'I don't like it. I'd like it less if I disobeyed him.' She makes a small sign, and the guards close the door.".
  Action explain_no_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Margravine you come without the Margrave's letter, and why the Prince is with you" {
    Speaker berengar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, or_hall) and at(berengar, or_hall) and e3Burned(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert e3Explained(rierdan). Assert e3Escape(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert e3TurnedAway(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
    Result "You say that you were given a letter and that it burned, and who gave it, and what it asked, and that the Prince is here to be out of the house it came from. The Margravine puts down her pen. 'That is a very odd cover story,' she says, 'for a truth. Sit down. You will want ham.'".
    Otherwise "'A letter that burned,' says the Margravine. 'On the road. With a prince in your company. I have not heard a story I liked less.' She has you shown to the gate, politely, and the gate is shut behind you. The Prince looks back at it once.".
  }
  Observe e3_confessed_told at hm_hall when e3Confessed(rierdan) and e3Letter(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "The Margrave has not met anyone's eye since the chapel. The letter was written that night, in a steady hand, by a man who has been shown himself and would rather not have been; it is the courteous page, and the seal is green.".
  Observe e3_explained_told near berengar when e3Explained(rierdan) "The Margravine of Orlay has put the Prince at her right hand, and the company at the end of the table, and a ham between them. She is writing, with pleasure, to her neighbour; the letter is about the price of wool.".
  Observe e3_killed_told near tiernan when e3Killed(rierdan) "Word comes to the kitchen by evening: Sir Dunmow Spargo and Sir Cullen Quillan were taken to the yard at dusk. The Prince listens, and puts down his knife. 'I said yes,' he says. 'I'll have to carry it that I said yes.'".
  Observe e3_killed_trust near tiernan when e3Killed(rierdan) and tiernanTrust(party) "'You stood on the wall with me,' says the Prince, to you, 'and then you let me choose this. I do not know whether to thank you.'".
  Observe e3_killed_scorn near tiernan when e3Killed(rierdan) and tiernanScorn(party) and not tiernanTrust(party) "'You told me to wait, and watch, and be sure,' says the Prince. 'And then the first time I could act, you handed me the pen.'".
  Observe e3_killed_spies near tiernan when e3Killed(rierdan) and e3Spies(rierdan) "'You knew about them,' says the Prince. 'You knew before I did. That is why you let it be them.' He is not angry. He is tired.".
  Observe e3_bell_told near berengar when e3Bellerophon(rierdan) "The company is in the Orlay larder among the hams, behind a good oak door. The Margravine has sent down bread and a note: that she is very sorry, that it is in the letter, and that she will take it as a kindness if nobody tries the door before the week is out.".
  Observe or_larder_scene at or_larder when true "A cold stone room hung with hams and strings of onions, one window the width of a hand, and a bench. The door is oak and has a bar on the outside. Someone has left a loaf and a note.".
  Rule rp_bell_lock when e3Bellerophon(rierdan) and not e3Locked(rierdan) { Assert e3Locked(rierdan). Set e3LockedAt(rierdan) to watch(clock). Assert at(party, or_larder). }
  Rule rp_unlock_trust when e3Locked(rierdan) and not e3Unlocked(rierdan) and tiernanTrust(party) and watch(clock) >= e3LockedAt(rierdan) + 432 { Assert e3Unlocked(rierdan). }
  Rule rp_unlock_cook when e3Locked(rierdan) and not e3Unlocked(rierdan) and watch(clock) >= e3LockedAt(rierdan) + 1008 { Assert e3Unlocked(rierdan). }
  Action pick_larder_lock(actor: group, site: place) "Work the bar loose from inside, with a spoon and a great deal of patience" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, or_larder) and e3Locked(rierdan) and not e3Unlocked(rierdan) and not f_lock(rierdan).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, trapwork, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert e3Unlocked(rierdan). Assert e3Picked(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert f_lock(rierdan). }
    Result "The bar comes up out of its bracket with a sound like a cough. The corridor beyond is empty. Somewhere a cook is singing.".
    Otherwise "The spoon bends. Whoever fitted the bar knew something about spoons.".
  }
  Observe e3_picked_told at or_larder when e3Picked(rierdan) "The bar lies on the flags where you left it. Nobody has come to put it back.".
  Observe e3_bell_trust at or_larder when e3Bellerophon(rierdan) and e3Unlocked(rierdan) and not e3Picked(rierdan) and tiernanTrust(party) "On the third night the Prince knocks from the passage. 'I have told her I am my uncle's heir,' he says through the door, 'and that I will go home and be what she likes, if she lets the Players go. She is considering it.' His voice is level.".
  Observe e3_bell_cook at or_larder when e3Bellerophon(rierdan) and e3Unlocked(rierdan) and not e3Picked(rierdan) and not tiernanTrust(party) "On the seventh night the Orlay cook lets you out by the coal door, because, he says, she makes a thing of it every time, and keeps his eyes on the pot.".
  Observe e3_turned_told near tiernan when e3TurnedAway(rierdan) "The Prince walks back to Harrowmere beside the cart, in the dust, and does not speak until the first milestone. Then he says, 'Well. That is a thing I should have thought of myself.'".
  Observe e3_escape_told near tiernan when e3Escape(rierdan) and not e3Held(rierdan) "The Prince is in the kitchen at Orlay eating the Margravine's ham with both hands, in a borrowed coat, with the Players round him and the look of having, for the first time, got away.".
  Observe e3_escape_seized near tiernan when e3Seized(rierdan) "Behind the kitchen wall, a long way off, two young men are being reasonable at some guards. The Prince does not look round. 'They were my friends,' he says, 'in the sense that I knew where they were.'".
  Observe e3_escape_trust near tiernan when e3Escape(rierdan) and not e3Held(rierdan) and tiernanTrust(party) "'Take me with you,' says the Prince. 'You are the ones who stayed. I can fence, I can write, and I'll be dreadful at everything else.'".
  Observe e3_escape_lonely near tiernan when e3Escape(rierdan) and not e3Held(rierdan) and tiernanLonely(party) and not tiernanTrust(party) "'Here I am,' says the Prince, looking at the ham, 'somewhere else, and still a prince. It is not at all what I was afraid of.'".
  Observe e3_escape_scorn near tiernan when e3Escape(rierdan) and not e3Held(rierdan) and tiernanScorn(party) and not tiernanTrust(party) and not tiernanLonely(party) "'You told me to wait and be sure,' says the Prince, not unkindly, with his mouth full. 'It turns out that when one is sure, one is generally somewhere else.'".
  Observe e3_escape_spared near tiernan when e3Escape(rierdan) and not e3Held(rierdan) and e3Spared(rierdan) "The Prince sits a little apart. 'I had my sword out in the chapel,' he says. 'You took my sleeve. I have not decided whether to thank you.' He turns the ham over. 'I have not decided whether I wished you hadn't.'".
  Observe e3_mis_told near tiernan when e3Misdelivered(rierdan) "The Prince has heard the Margravine of Orlay's reply, which is a ham and an offer of marriage, and is lying on the ground at the gate of Orlay, laughing, with tears down his face. 'My uncle,' he says, 'has proposed to the wrong woman. The wrong woman has said yes.' He is quiet. 'It is the first time,' he says, 'that I have thought we might get out of this.'".
  Rule rp_grave when x3c(rierdan) and not e3Letter(rierdan) and not e3Grave(rierdan) and harm(rierdan) >= 3 and watch(clock) >= e3Start(rierdan) + 60 {
    Assert e3Grave(rierdan). Assert e3Done(rierdan). }
  Observe e3_grave_gate at hm_gate when e3Grave(rierdan) "A bell is going at the Margravate chapel, one stroke to a breath. The gate guard has taken his helmet off and does not seem to know where to put it.".
  Observe e3_grave_told at hm_hall when e3Grave(rierdan) "At the match the Margrave drinks to his nephew in a cup he does not drink from. The foil is not blunt. The Prince, who has been wounded twice already this month, goes down on the grass in the sun with his mother's name in his mouth. He has time to say 'Well,' and nothing more. In the chapel the stone Margrave has a new neighbour and the Margravine has the space for the next. The company plays that night because the Margrave commands it, and Swale does not remember a word.".
  Milestone m_prince_ghost "heard the Margrave's ghost on the rampart" worth 150 when e3Ghost(party).
  Milestone m_prince_letter "read what the letter said" worth 150 when e3Read(rierdan).
  Milestone m_prince_done "came away from Harrowmere" worth 300 when e3Done(rierdan).
  // Dorcas plays the Margravine as she decided to play the Lady at Cairnholt (the answer given in "The Three" is read here).
  Topic dorcas_iseult_a with dorcas "Ask Dorcas how she plays the Margravine, now" when e3Done(rierdan) and dorcasWants(party) once {
    Says "'Cleanly,' says Dorcas. 'She wanted the throne and the husband and she got both and it has not been enough. I did the Lady that way too, you remember, and I was right. I am a little ashamed how easily it comes.'".
  }
  Topic dorcas_iseult_b with dorcas "Ask Dorcas how she plays the Margravine, now" when e3Done(rierdan) and dorcasAfraid(party) once {
    Says "'The same way as the Lady,' says Dorcas. 'I find I can only do them frightened. Iseult is so still because if she moved she would have to choose between her son and her husband. It makes the part quiet. Gosse says nobody will hear me past the third row.' She smiles. 'The third row will.'".
  }
  Chapter ch_prince "The Prince and the Letter" when e3On(rierdan) and not e3Done(rierdan) "A Margravate in mourning, a prince who will not be guarded, a ghost on the rampart, a letter you have not yet been given.".
  Relation f_capt(place).
  Relation e3Locked(place).
  Relation e3Unlocked(place).
  Relation e3Picked(place).
  Relation e3Held(place).
  Relation e3Exposed(place).
  Relation e3Dismissed(place).
  Relation e3ForgeBlown(place).
  Relation e3SheetTaken(place).
  Relation f_conf(place).
  Relation f_lock(place).
}
